From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn-patches <tyn-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:32:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: STEINS;GATE 0 system menu and save / load screen

The S;G0 system menu (the scene shrinks into a monitor, twelve round
buttons) and its save / load / quick load screen are ported from Game.exe
the same way as the phone: translated from the Ghidra decompile
(tools/impacto/sg0/translate_phone.py now also takes 0x4571d0, 0x4579e0,
0x457b80, 0x457bc0 and the save screen 0x454e00..0x456940 with the number
and ASCII text helpers it uses).

- 00:44 (0x482760) and 10:23 (0x485f10) for InstructionSet::SG0; their
  layer is drawn on the SystemMenu draw component after its menus (the
  save screen over the title menu). The engine system menu and save menu
  classes are off in the sg0-pc profile (Type None).
- savemenu.cpp: the save headers the screen reads come from the engine's
  save system (status, date, play time, title, write protection); quick
  saves listed newest first; thumbnails are the engine's.
- The screen is taken once when the menu opens (render target 8 as a
  surface); the click that opens a screen does not count on it.
- The phone's tables (10:37 00, run once at start) are no longer wiped by
  the new game / load reset.
- sg0-pc: FramebufferAlpha, the menu sheets as script handled sheets.

Verified on MuMu (Android 15 x86_64 emulator, not a real device), sg0-pc
(Steam data, Chinese): system menu opens / closes; SAVE writes slot 1 and 2
with thumbnail, chapter title, play time and date; LOAD from the system menu
and from the title (CONTINUE > LOAD) with the confirmation; the game goes on
after loading.

